    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked that on a successful owner create, the app enqueue a welcome notification by emitting a line via the logger named `NOTIFY` containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nI edited `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")`), mirroring the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n2. Added an `enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner owner)` method that emits a single line carrying `ownerId` and `memberId` (routed through the existing `primaryIdentifier` accessor, so the notion of the owner's identity stays in one place alongside the audit trail).\n3. Called it in `addOwner`, right after the owner is persisted and the audit trail is emitted.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and its `memberId` \u2014 passes:\n\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - welcome notification queued ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n...\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```",
